    <help format="markdown"><![CDATA[
# What it does

3Dtrees: Inventory measures every tree of one or more instance segmentations of
a point cloud: stem position and diameter at breast height (DBH) from circles
fitted to stem slices, height above the terrain, crown area and species. It
uses the forest inventory of CspStandSegmentation unchanged and can also create
a comparative shortest path (CSP) segmentation. The method and every column are
described in the [tool README](https://github.com/3dTrees-earth/3dtrees_CSP_StandSegmentation#readme).

# Input

- **Segmented point cloud**: one full-resolution LAS/LAZ or COPC file with a
  CRS projected in metres and the instance dimensions to inventory.
- **Segmentation**: one block per instance dimension (for example
  `PredInstance_SAT`, `PredInstance_FM`), optionally with its species ID and
  probability dimensions. Each dimension only once.
- **CSP segmentation** (default No): Yes adds a `PredInstance_CSP`
  segmentation, seeded from point density or a supplied seed table. CSP keeps
  the whole cloud in memory, so use it for plot-sized clouds.
- **Extra attributes**: `PredScore_FM,PredSemantic_FM` adds the ForestMamba
  scores and wood and leaf counts.
- **Terrain model**: generated (existing ground class, else cloth simulation)
  or a supplied GeoTIFF covering the cloud.
- **Area of interest** and **Species names** are optional.
- **Advanced parameters**: the stem slices, the DBH fit and the measurement
  grid. DBH, height, crown and position are measured on one point per tree
  and 1 cm cell; point counts and species use every point.

CPU and memory come from the Galaxy job allocation.

# Outputs

- **Inventory** (CSV) and **Inventory (Parquet)**: the same table, one row per
  tree and segmentation, with the DBH fit quality, every DBH run (`dbh_fits`),
  the stem slices (`dbh_slices`) and the crown polygon (`crown_hull`, GeoJSON).
- **Stand summary**: one row per segmentation with stand area, trees per
  hectare, DBH and height statistics and the coordinate reference system.
- **DTM**, and its crop to the area of interest when one is given.
- With CSP: the input point cloud with every dimension plus `PredInstance_CSP`.
  The CSP rows of the inventory carry the seed each tree grew from
  (`seed_x`, `seed_y`, `seed_height_m`).
    ]]></help>
